  "goodToKnow": "Schimmeln means to go mouldy: Das Brot schimmelt, Die Marmelade ist geschimmelt. Der Schimmel is mould, a frequent problem in German flats due to poor ventilation; tenants are told to air rooms regularly (Stoßlüften). Confusingly, der Schimmel is also a white horse, so ein weißer Schimmel is the classic German example of a redundant phrase. Schimmelig means mouldy. Perfect with sein or haben."
